<worksheet >
    <title>MD-1 Matrix Operations</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all eight parts. 
      Complete any six parts to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <introduction><p>Given the following matrices:<md alignment="alignat" alignat-columns="3">
            <mrow>A=\begin{bmatrix}1 &amp; 3&amp; -2\\ 5 &amp; 0 &amp; 4\end{bmatrix}, 
              B= \begin{bmatrix} 2 &amp; -1\\3 &amp; 6\end{bmatrix}, C=\begin{bmatrix} -5 &amp; 2\\ 0 &amp; 1\end{bmatrix},
              D=\begin{bmatrix} 4 &amp; 1\\-2 &amp; 3\\ 0 &amp; -1\end{bmatrix}</mrow>
            </md> Compute the following matrices, if possible.  If the computation is not 
            possible, explain why.</p></introduction>
      <task><statement><p><m>BC</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>A^T+D</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>C^{-1}</m></p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p><m>A+B</m></p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>